# FBM retrieval-relevance metric — P@5 (Slice F, final)

Per `docs/plans/fbm-retrieval-relevance-metric-p-at-5.md` and the
owner-greenlit unified plan
`workspace/.scratch/claude-output/loam-fbm-quality-and-accuracy-unified-plan.md`
(Slice F; Luke 13582). Single-component amendment on the EXISTING primary-persona
component — the FINAL slice of the FBM quality-and-accuracy overhaul. Read-only
against the live FBM store/corpus.

A BrainBench-style precision-at-5 (P@5) retrieval-quality METRIC + a sealed
regression-guard test, so relevance quality cannot silently rot after the A-E
changes (write-gate, load-filter, per-project STATE, lens injection, multi-repo
visibility). The metric MEASURES the production retrieval — the sealed
`index.search` (corpus BM25) + `_episode_hits` (episode store) + `_merge_by_score`
(salience gate + absolute floor + dedup + weight/salience boost + top-N) pipeline
that `retrieve()` runs — over a HONEST labeled probe set, and a sealed test asserts
the live retrieval clears a CONSERVATIVE P@5 floor. P@5 = (# of the top-5 surfaced
hits that are labeled-relevant) / 5, averaged over the probe set.

The honesty problem (named + resolved — the whole point of the metric): a
relevance metric whose labels are reverse-engineered from the ranker passes by
construction and guards nothing (a tautology). Resolution: relevance is defined by
AUTHORED TOPIC MEMBERSHIP, decided BEFORE any ranking is run — each probe's
relevant set is the doc/episode signatures authored into that probe's topic, plus
deliberate DISTRACTORS (off-topic docs, junk-salience episodes) that share surface
tokens but are NOT topically relevant. A ranker that surfaces a distractor in the
top-5 LOWERS P@5 — the regression signal the metric exists to catch. The floor is
CONSERVATIVE (a margin below the honestly-measured value) and the ranker is
DETERMINISTIC (per-source min-max + weight/salience boost, sorted on
(-boosted, arrival_index) — a total order, no randomness / no embeddings / no
clock), so noise cannot flip the guard red; the metric verifies determinism by
running twice and comparing.

Ruthless-Feedback pre-commitment honored: the floor was set at/below the honestly
measured P@5; a low value would have been surfaced, never floored-up, and the
labels were never edited to match ranker output.

Reuse, not re-implement (Lens 1/2, Tier-0 at build time): the metric drives the
SAME `index.search` + `_episode_hits` + `_merge_by_score` the production
`retrieve()` runs. A new `keep_pace/retrieval_metric.py` adds:
  - `rank(...)` — the production-faithful ranked accessor: runs the EXACT steps
    `retrieve()` runs (trivial-skip, fresh objectives, work-anchor, corpus search,
    episode hits, merge) and returns the ordered merged hit list PRE-render.
    `retrieve()` is refactored to delegate to `rank()` + `_render_injection` so the
    metric measures the same code path that ships (no drift between measured and
    shipped) — a byte-identical refactor verified by the pre-existing KP1 / FBMU /
    FBM-FILTER suite staying green.
  - `Probe(query, relevant, last_topic)` + `P5Report(mean, per_probe, k,
    num_probes)` frozen dataclasses.
  - `precision_at_k(probes, config, *, k=5, ...)` — runs `rank()` per probe, takes
    the top-k, counts how many carry a relevance signature in the probe's authored
    relevant set, divides by k, averages over probes. Deterministic.
The controlled probe FIXTURE (topical clusters + distractors + authored relevant
sets) lives in the TEST — the module is the reusable metric; the fixture is the
honest labeled set. Episodes are seeded through the REAL `write_episode` ingest so
salience is computed by production, not hand-stamped; the corpus fixture is plain
`*.md` indexed via the existing `discover_corpus`.

ACs (each → a named test; >=1 outcome-altitude):
  - AC.FBM-P5-METRIC.1 (F1) — over a controlled probe fixture (topical clusters +
    distractors, relevance labeled on topic not on ranker output) the metric
    computes a P@5 number that clears a conservative floor with the salience gate
    ACTIVE, and DROPS below the floor under a SEEDED regression (junk re-admitted
    by dropping the gate to 0.0) — the guard fires.
    (`test_AC_FBM_P5_METRIC_1_honest_p_at_5_and_seeded_regression.py`.)
  - AC.FBM-P5-METRIC.2 (F2) — two runs over the same probes + config produce
    IDENTICAL reports (determinism verified), AND a probe scores STRICTLY below 1.0
    in the presence of an unfiltered distractor (the labels are independent of the
    ranker — a tautological set would force 1.0).
    (`test_AC_FBM_P5_METRIC_2_deterministic_and_non_tautological.py`.)
  - AC.FBM-P5-METRIC.S (F3, outcome-altitude) — the REAL metric end-to-end over the
    PRODUCTION retrieval against the LIVE FBM store + corpus, NO pre-arranged
    scores, probe relevance authored on genuine topical relevance to known durable
    corpus topics: produces an ACTUAL P@5 number from real `rank()` and asserts it
    clears the conservative sealed floor. A STUB-class test (mocked rank / hand-fed
    hits) does NOT satisfy this. Skips cleanly if the live store is absent. Measured
    live P@5 recorded in §14.
    (`test_AC_FBM_P5_METRIC_S_live_retrieval_p_at_5_floor.py`.)

